msgstr "*リリース日: 2021-04-05*"

#: ../NEWS:33533
msgid ""
":issue:`42988`: :cve:`2021-3426`: Remove the ``getfile`` feature of the :mod:"
"`pydoc` module which could be abused to read arbitrary files on the disk "
"(directory traversal vulnerability). Moreover, even source code of Python "
"modules can contain sensitive data like passwords. Vulnerability reported by "
"David Schwörer."
msgstr ""

#: ../NEWS:33539
msgid ""
":issue:`43285`: :mod:`ftplib` no longer trusts the IP address value returned "
"from the server in response to the PASV command by default.  This prevents a "
"malicious FTP server from using the response to probe IPv4 address and port "
"combinations on the client network."
msgstr ""

#: ../NEWS:33544
msgid ""
"Code that requires the former vulnerable behavior may set a "
"``trust_server_pasv_ipv4_address`` attribute on their :class:`ftplib.FTP` "
"instances to ``True`` to re-enable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../NEWS:33548
msgid ""
":issue:`43439`: Add audit hooks for :func:`gc.get_objects`, :func:`gc."
"get_referrers` and :func:`gc.get_referents`. Patch by Pablo Galindo."
msgstr ""

